{
  "title": "17: al-Israa الإسراء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nسُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْۤ اَسْرٰى بِعَبْدِهٖ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَا الَّذِىْ بٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهٗ لِنُرِيَهٗ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(1)\nLAAHE LAZEE AASRAA BEA’ABDEH LAYLAN MENAL MASJEDIL HARAAME ELAL MASJEDIL AL-AAQSAA LAZEE BAARAKNAA HAWLAHU LENUREEH MIN AAYAATENAA INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nGlory to (Allah) Who did take His servant for a Journey by night from the Sacred Mosque to the farthest Mosque, whose precincts We did bless, in order that We might show him some of Our Signs: for He is the One Who heareth and seeth (all things). \nوَاٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَ جَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَلَّا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِىْ وَكِيْلًا ؕ‏(2)\nWA AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA LAW HODAM LLEBANEAA ISRAAA-EELAZ ALLAA TATTAKHEZOOA MIN DOONEAA WAKEELAA.\nWe gave Moses the Book, and made it a Guide to the Children of Israel, (commanding): “Take not other than Me as Disposer of (your) affairs.” \nذُرِّيَّةَ مَنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَبْدًا شَكُوْرًا‏(3)\nZURREETA MAN HAMALNAA LAAHA NOOHIN INNAHU KAANA A’BDAN SHAKOORAN.\nO ye that are sprung from those whom We carried (in the Ark) with Noah! Verily he was a devotee most grateful. \nوَقَضَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ لَتُفْسِدُنَّ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَّتَيْنِ وَلَتَعْلُنَّ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(4)\nWA QAZAYNAA ELAA BANEE AESRAAEELA FIL KETAABE LATUFSEDUNNA FIL ARZE MARRATAYNE WALATAA’LUNNA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nAnd We gave (Clear) Warning to the Children of Israel in the Book, that twice would they do mischief on the earth and be elated with mighty arrogance (and twice would they be punished)! \nفَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ اُوْلٰٮهُمَا بَعَثْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ عِبَادًا لَّنَاۤ اُولِىْ بَاْسٍ شَدِيْدٍ فَجَاسُوْا خِلٰلَ الدِّيَارِ ؕ وَكَانَ وَعْدًا مَّفْعُوْلًا‏(5)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AOOLAAHUMAA BAA’ASNAA A’LAYKUM E’EBAADAN LANAA OOLEE OOLOO BAA-SIN FAJAASOOA KHELAALA AD-DEEARE KAANAL WA’DAN MMAFU’OOLAN.\nWhen the first of the warnings came to pass, We sent against you Our servants given to terrible warfare: They entered the very inmost parts of your homes; and it was a warning (completely) fulfilled. \nثُمَّ رَدَدْنَا لَكُمُ الْكَرَّةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاَمْدَدْنٰكُمْ بِاَمْوَالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ وَجَعَلْنٰكُمْ اَكْثَرَ نَفِيْرًا‏(6)\nSUMMA RADADNAA LAKOMUL AL-KARRATA A’LAYHIM WAAMDADNAAKUM BEAAMWAALIN WWABANEENA WA JA-A’LNAAKUM AKSARAN NAFEERAN.\nThen did We grant you the Return as against them: We gave you increase in resources and sons, and made you the more numerous in man-power. \nاِنْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْوَاِنْ اَسَاْتُمْ فَلَهَا ؕ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ لِيَسُوْۤءا وُجُوْهَكُمْ وَلِيَدْخُلُوا الْمَسْجِدَ كَمَا دَخَلُوْهُ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّلِيُتَبِّرُوْا مَا عَلَوْا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(7)\nIN AAHSANTUM AAHSANTUM LEAANFUSEKUMWAAN AASAATUM FA LAHAA FA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AAKHERATE LEESOOA WOJOOHAKUM WALEEDKHULOOA MASJEDIL KAMAA DAKHALOOHU AWWALA MARRAH WWALEETABBEROOA MAA A’ALAWA TATBEERAN.\nIf ye did well, ye did well for yourselves; if ye did evil, (ye did it) against yourselves. So when the second of the warnings came to pass, (We permitted your enemies) to disfigure your faces, and to enter your Temple as they had entered it before, and to visit with destruction all that fell into their power. \nعَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يَّرْحَمَكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ عُدْتُّمْ عُدْنَاۘ وَجَعَلْنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ حَصِيْرًا‏(8)\nA’SAA RABBOKUM AN YYARHAMAKUM WA U’UDTTUM U’UDNAA WA JA-A’LNAA JAHANNAMA LIL KAAFEREENA HASEERAN.\nIt may be that your Lord may (yet) show Mercy unto you; but if ye revert (to your sins), We shall revert (to Our punishments): And we have made Hell a prison for those who reject (all Faith). \nاِنَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ يَهْدِىْ لِلَّتِىْ هِىَ اَقْوَمُ وَ يُبَشِّرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ اَنَّ لَهُمْ اَجْرًا كَبِيْرًا ۙ‏(9)\nINNA HAAZAL QURAANA YAHDEE LELLATEAA HEYA AAQWAMU WA YUBASSHERU MOAMENEEN LAZEENA YA’MALOON SAALEHAATE ANNAL LAHUM AJRAN KABEERAA.\nVerily this Qur'an doth guide to that which is most right (or stable), and giveth the Glad Tidings to the Believers who work deeds of righteousness, that they shall have a magnificent reward; \nوَّاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا‏(10)\nWA ANNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd to those who believe not in the Hereafter, (it announceth) that We have prepared for them a Penalty Grievous (indeed). \nوَيَدْعُ الْاِنْسَانُ بِالشَّرِّ دُعَآءَهٗ بِالْخَيْرِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ عَجُوْلًا‏(11)\nWAYADU’U INSAANO BEALSSHARRE DUA’AAAH BE-KHAYR KAANAL INSAANO A’AJOOLAN.\nThe prayer that man should make for good, he maketh for evil; for man is given to hasty (deeds). \nوَجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ اٰيَتَيْنِ فَمَحَوْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ الَّيْلِ وَجَعَلْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ النَّهَارِ مُبْصِرَةً لِّتَبْتَغُوْا فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِيْنَ وَالْحِسَابَؕ وَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ تَفْصِيْلًا‏(12)\nWA JA-A’LNAA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA AAAYATAYNE FAMAHAWNAA AAYATA LAYLE WA JA-A’LNAA AAYATA AN-NAHAARE MUBSERATAN LLETABTAGHOOA FAZLAM MIR RABBEKUM WALETAA’LAMOOA A’ADADA AS-SENEENA WAL HESAABA WA KULLA SHAY-IN FASSALNAAHU TAFSEELAN.\nWe have made the Night and the Day as two (of Our) Signs: the Sign of the Night have We obscured, while the Sign of the Day We have made to enlighten you; that ye may seek bounty from your Lord, and that ye may know the number and count of the years: all things have We explained in detail. \nوَكُلَّ اِنْسَانٍ اَلْزَمْنٰهُ طٰۤئِرَهٗ فِىْ عُنُقِهٖؕ وَنُخْرِجُ لَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ كِتٰبًا يَّلْقٰٮهُ مَنْشُوْرًا‏(13)\nWA KULLA AENSAANIN AALZAMNAAHU TAAERAH FEE U’UNUQEH WANUKHREJU LAHU YAWMA QEYAAMATE KETAABAA YYALQAAHU MANSHOORAN.\nEvery man's fate We have fastened on his own neck: On the Day of Judgment We shall bring out for him a scroll, which he will see spread open. \nاِقْرَاْ كِتٰبَك َؕ كَفٰى بِنَفْسِكَ الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكَ حَسِيْبًا ؕ‏(14)\nIQRAA KETAABAK KAFAA BE-TUKHFEE YAWMA A’LAYKA HASEEBAA.\n(It will be said to him:) “Read thine (own) record: Sufficient is thy soul this day to make out an account against thee.” \nمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖ ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا ؕ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى ؕ وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِيْنَ حَتّٰى نَبْعَثَ رَسُوْلًا‏(15)\nMANIS TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEHI WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU WA MAA KUNNAA MUA’AZZEBEENA HATTAA NABA’ASA RASOOLAM.\nWho receiveth guidance, receiveth it for his own benefit: who goeth astray doth so to his own loss: No bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another: nor would We visit with Our Wrath until We had sent an messenger (to give warning). \nوَاِذَاۤ اَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ نُّهْلِكَ قَرْيَةً اَمَرْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهَا فَفَسَقُوْا فِيْهَا فَحَقَّ عَلَيْهَا الْقَوْلُ فَدَمَّرْنٰهَا تَدْمِيْرًا‏(16)\nWA EZAA AARADNAA AN NNUHLEKA QARYATAN AAMARNAA MUTRAFEEHAA FAFASAQOOA FEEHAA FA HAQQA A’LAYHAA QAWLO FADAMMARNAAHAA TADMEERAN.\nWhen We decide to destroy a population, We (first) send a definite order to those among them who are given the good things of this life and yet transgress; so that the word is proved true against them: then (it is) We destroy them utterly. \nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ نُوْحٍؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(17)\nWA AHLAKNAL MENAL QOROONE MIN BA’DE NOOHIN KAFAA BERABBEKA BEZUNOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nHow many generations have We destroyed after Noah? and enough is thy Lord to note and see the sins of His servants. \nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْعَاجِلَةَ عَجَّلْنَا لَهٗ فِيْهَا مَا نَشَآءُ لِمَنْ نُّرِيْدُ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَۚ يَصْلٰٮهَا مَذْمُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(18)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO A’AJELATA A’AJJALNAA LAHU FEEHAA MAA NASHAAA-O LEMAN-Y NNUREEDU SUMMA JA-A’LNAA LAHU JAHANNAMA YASLAAHAA MAZMOOMAN MMADHOORAN.\nIf any do wish for the transitory things (of this life), We readily grant them - such things as We will, to such person as We will: in the end have We provided Hell for them: they will burn therein, disgraced and rejected. \nوَمَنْ اَرَادَ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَسَعٰى لَهَا سَعْيَهَا وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ سَعْيُهُمْ مَّشْكُوْرًا‏(19)\nWA MAN ARAADA AAKHERATA MOH LAHAA SAA’YAHAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FAAWLAAEKA KAANA SAA’YUHUM MASHKOORAA.\nThose who do wish for the (things of) the Hereafter, and strive therefor with all due striving, and have Faith, they are the ones whose striving is acceptable (to Allah). \nكُلًّا نُّمِدُّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مِنْ عَطَآءِ رَبِّكَ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ عَطَآءُ رَبِّكَ مَحْظُوْرًا‏(20)\nKULLAN NNUMEDDU HAAOOLAAA-E WA HAAOOLAAA-E MIN A’ATAAE RABBEKA WA MAA KAANA A’ATAAU RABBEKA MAHZOORAN.\nOf the bounties of thy Lord We bestow freely on all- These as well as those: The bounties of thy Lord are not closed (to anyone). \nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ ؕ وَلَلْاٰخِرَةُ اَكْبَرُ دَرَجٰتٍ وَّاَكْبَرُ تَفْضِيْلًا‏(21)\nAUNZUR KAYFA FAZZALNAA BA’ZAHUM A’LAA ELAA WA LAL-AAKHERATO AKBARO DARAJAATIN WWAAKBARU TAFZEELAN.\nSee how We have bestowed more on some than on others; but verily the Hereafter is more in rank and gradation and more in excellence. \nلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَقْعُدَ مَذْمُوْمًا مَّخْذُوْلًا‏(22)\nLAA TAJ-A’L LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FATAQU’UDA MAZMOOMAN MMAKHZOOLAN.\nTake not with Allah another object of worship; or thou (O man!) wilt sit in disgrace and destitution. \nوَقَضٰى رَبُّكَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا ؕ اِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِنْدَكَ الْكِبَرَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَوْ كِلٰهُمَا فَلَا تَقُلْ لَّهُمَاۤ اُفٍّ وَّلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا وَقُلْ لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِيْمًا‏(23)\nWA QAZAA RABBOKA ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA IYYAAHO WA BIL-WAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW IMMAA YABLUGHANNA E’ENDAKA AL-KEBARA AAHADUHUMAA AW KELAAHUMAA FALAA TAQUL LAHOMAA AUFFIN WA LAA TANHARHUMAA WA QUL LAHOMAA QAWLAM KAREEMAA.\nThy Lord hath decreed that ye worship none but Him, and that ye be kind to parents. Whether one or both of them attain old age in thy life, say not to them a word of contempt, nor repel them, but address them in terms of honour. \nوَاخْفِضْ لَهُمَا جَنَاحَ الذُّلِّ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ ارْحَمْهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيٰنِىْ صَغِيْرًا ؕ‏(24)\nWAAKHFEZ LAHOMAA JANAAHA AZ-ZULLE MENAL AR-RAHMATE WA QUL RABBIL ARHAMHUMAA KAMAA RABBAYNEAA AW.\nAnd, out of kindness, lower to them the wing of humility, and say: “My Lord! bestow on them thy Mercy even as they cherished me in childhood.” \nرَّبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْ نُفُوْسِكُمْؕ اِنْ تَكُوْنُوْا صٰلِحِيْنَ فَاِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِلْاَوَّابِيْنَ غَفُوْرًا‏(25)\nRRABBUKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE NUFOOSEKUM IN TAKOONOO SAALEHEENA FA-INNAHU KAANA LIL-AAWABEENA GHAFOORAR.\nYour Lord knoweth best what is in your hearts: If ye do deeds of righteousness, verily He is Most Forgiving to those who turn to Him again and again (in true penitence). \nوَاٰتِ ذَا الْقُرْبٰى حَقَّهٗ وَالْمِسْكِيْنَ وَابْنَ السَّبِيْلِ وَلَا تُبَذِّرْ تَبْذِيْرًا‏(26)\nWAATE ZAL QURBAA HAQQAHU WA MISKEENA WAB SABEELE WA LAA TUBAZZER TABZEERAN.\nAnd render to the kindred their due rights, as (also) to those in want, and to the wayfarer: But squander not (your wealth) in the manner of a spendthrift. \nاِنَّ الْمُبَذِّرِيْنَ كَانُوْۤا اِخْوَانَ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِرَبِّهٖ كَفُوْرًا‏(27)\nINNAL AL-MUBAZZEREENA KAANOO AEKHWAANA ASH-SHAYTEENE KAANAL SHAYTAANO LE-RABBEHI KAFOORAA.\nVerily spendthrifts are brothers of the Evil Ones; and the Evil One is to his Lord (himself) ungrateful. \nوَاِمَّا تُعْرِضَنَّ عَنْهُمُ ابْتِغَآءَ رَحْمَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ تَرْجُوْهَا فَقُلْ لَّهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّيْسُوْرًا‏(28)\nWA AMMAA TUA’REZANNA A’NHOMUL TEGHAAA-A RAHMATIN MIR RABBEKA TARJOOHAA FAQUL LAHUM QAWLAM MMAYSOORAN.\nAnd even if thou hast to turn away from them in pursuit of the Mercy from thy Lord which thou dost expect, yet speak to them a word of easy kindness. \nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ يَدَكَ مَغْلُوْلَةً اِلٰى عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبْسُطْهَا كُلَّ الْبَسْطِ فَتَقْعُدَ مَلُوْمًا مَّحْسُوْرًا‏(29)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’L YADAKA MAGHLOOLATAN ELAA U’UNUQEKA WA LAA TABSUTHAA KULLA AL-BASTE FATAQU’UDA MALOOMAN MMAHSOORAN.\nMake not thy hand tied (like a niggard's) to thy neck, nor stretch it forth to its utmost reach, so that thou become blameworthy and destitute. \nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(30)\nINNAL RABBAKA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nVerily thy Lord doth provide sustenance in abundance for whom He pleaseth, and He provideth in a just measure. For He doth know and regard all His servants. \nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَكُمْ خَشْيَةَ اِمْلَاقٍؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَاِيَّاكُمْؕ اِنَّ قَتْلَهُمْ كَانَ خِطْاً كَبِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA LAA TAQTULOOA AWLAADAKUM KHASHYATA AEMLAAQIN NAHNO NARZUQUHUM WAAYYAAKUM INNAL QATLAHUM KAANA KHETAAN KABEERAA.\nKill not your children for fear of want: We shall provide sustenance for them as well as for you. Verily the killing of them is a great sin. \nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الزِّنٰٓى اِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً  ؕ وَسَآءَ سَبِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA AZ-ZENAAA INNAHU KAANA FAAHESHATAN WA SAAA-A SABEELAA.\nNor come nigh to adultery: for it is a shameful (deed) and an evil, opening the road (to other evils). \nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَمَنْ قُتِلَ مَظْلُوْمًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِيِّهٖ سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا يُسْرِفْ فِّى الْقَتْلِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مَنْصُوْرًا‏(33)\nWA LAA TAQTULOOA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA MAN QOTELAL MAZLOOMAN FAQAD JA-A’LNAA LEWALIYYEHI SULTAANAN FALAA YUSREF FFEAA QATL INNAHU KAANA MANSOORAN.\nNor take life - which Allah has made sacred - except for just cause. And if anyone is slain wrongfully, we have given his heir authority (to demand qisas or to forgive): but let him not exceed bounds in the matter of taking life; for he is helped (by the Law). \nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوْا مَالَ الْيَتِيْمِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَاَوْفُوْا بِالْعَهْدِۚ اِنَّ الْعَهْدَ كَانَ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(34)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA MAALA AL-YATEEME ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO HATTAA HATTAA ASHUDDAHU WA AWFOO BIL-A’AHDE INNAL AL-A’AHDA KAANA MAS-OOLAA.\nCome not nigh to the orphan's property except to improve it, until he attains the age of full strength; and fulfil (every) engagement, for (every) engagement will be enquired into (on the Day of Reckoning). \nوَاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ اِذَا كِلْتُمْ وَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَحْسَنُ تَاْوِيْلًا‏(35)\nWAAWFOOA AL-KAYLA EZAA KELTUM WAZENOOA BIL-QESTAASE AL-MUSTAQEEME ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL WWAAHSANU TAAWEELAN.\nGive full measure when ye measure, and weigh with a balance that is straight: that is the most fitting and the most advantageous in the final determination. \nوَلَا تَقْفُ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنَّ السَّمْعَ وَالْبَصَرَ وَالْفُؤَادَ كُلُّ اُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ عَنْهُ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(36)\nWA LAA TAQFU MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUM INNAL JA-A’LA WA BASARA WAL FUAADA KULLO AOOLAAEKA KAANA A’NHO MAS-OOLAA.\nAnd pursue not that of which thou hast no knowledge; for every act of hearing, or of seeing or of (feeling in) the heart will be enquired into (on the Day of Reckoning). \nوَلَا تَمْشِ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَحًا ۚ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَخْرِقَ الْاَرْضَ وَلَنْ تَبْلُغَ الْجِبَالَ طُوْلًا‏(37)\nWA LAA TAMSHE FIL ARZE MARAHAN INNAKA LAN TAKHREQA ARZA WA LAN TABLUGHA JEBAALA TOOLAN.\nNor walk on the earth with insolence: for thou canst not rend the earth asunder, nor reach the mountains in height. \nكُلُّ ذٰ لِكَ كَانَ سَيِّئُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ مَكْرُوْهًا‏(38)\nKULLO ZAA LEKA KAANA SAYUH I’NDAL RABBEKA MAKROOHAN.\nOf all such things the evil is hateful in the sight of thy Lord. \nذٰ لِكَ مِمَّاۤ اَوْحٰۤى اِلَيْكَ رَبُّكَ مِنَ الْحِكْمَةِ ؕ وَلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتُلْقٰى فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَلُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(39)\nZAA LEKA MIMMAA AAWHAA ELAYKA RABBOKA MENAL AL-HEKMATE WA LAA TAJ-A’L LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FATULQAA FEE JAHANNAMA MALOOMAN MMADHOORAN.\nThese are among the (precepts of) wisdom, which thy Lord has revealed to thee. Take not, with Allah, another object of worship, lest thou shouldst be thrown into Hell, blameworthy and rejected. \nاَفَاَصْفٰٮكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِالْبَنِيْنَ وَ اتَّخَذَ مِنَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنَاثًا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَقُوْلُوْنَ قَوْلًا عَظِيْمًا‏(40)\nAAFAASFAAKUM RABBOKUM BIL-BANEENA WA TAKHAZA MENAL AL-MALAAEKATE AENAASAN INNAKUM LATAQOOLOONA QAWLAM A’ZEEMAA.\nHas then your Lord (O Pagans!) preferred for you sons, and taken for Himself daughters among the angels? Truly ye utter a most dreadful saying! \nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ؕ وَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا نُفُوْرًا‏(41)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA FEE HAAZAL QUR-AANE LEEZZAKKAROOA WA MAA YAZEEDUHUM ILLAA NUFOORAN.\nWe have explained (things) in various (ways) in this Qur'an, in order that they may receive admonition, but it only increases their flight (from the Truth)! \nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ مَعَهٗۤ اٰلِهَةٌ كَمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذًا لَّابْتَغَوْا اِلٰى ذِى الْعَرْشِ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nQUL LAW KAANA MA-A’HU AAALEHATUN KAMAA YAQOOLOONA EZAL LLAABTAGHAWA ELAA ZIL A’RSHIL SABEELAA.\nSay: If there had been (other) gods with Him, as they say, behold, they would certainly have sought out a way to the Lord of the Throne! \nسُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(43)\nWALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YAQOOLOONA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nGlory to Him! He is high above all that they say!- Exalted and Great (beyond measure)! \nتُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمٰوٰتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّؕ وَاِنْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تَفْقَهُوْنَ تَسْبِيْحَهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حَلِيْمًا غَفُوْرًا‏(44)\nTUSABBEHU LAHUL AS-SAMAAWAATU AS-SABU’U WAL WA MAN FEEHENNA WA MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA YOSABBEHO BEHAMDEH WA LAAKIL LAA TAFQAHOONA TASBEEHAHUM INNAHU KAANA HALEEMAA GHAFOORAR.\nThe seven heavens and the earth, and all beings therein, declare His glory: there is not a thing but celebrates His praise; And yet ye understand not how they declare His glory! Verily He is Oft-Forbear, Most Forgiving! \nوَاِذَا قَرَاْتَ الْقُرْاٰنَ جَعَلْنَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ حِجَابًا مَّسْتُوْرًا ۙ‏(45)\nWA EZAA QARAATA QURAANA JA-A’LNAA WA WA BAYNA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE HEJAABAN MMASTOORAN.\nWhen thou dost recite the Qur'an, We put, between thee and those who believe not in the Hereafter, a veil invisible: \nوَّجَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا ؕ وَاِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ وَحْدَهٗ وَلَّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهِمْ نُفُوْرًا‏(46)\nWA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AAKENNATAN AN YYAFQAHOOHU WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAN WA EZAA ZAKARTA RABBAKA FIL QUR-AANE WAHDAH WALLAW A’LAA AADBAAREHEM NUFOORAN.\nAnd We put coverings over their hearts (and minds) lest they should understand the Qur'an, and deafness into their ears: when thou dost commemorate thy Lord and Him alone in the Qur'an, they turn on their backs, fleeing (from the Truth). \nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ بِهٖۤ اِذْ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِذْ هُمْ نَجْوٰٓى اِذْ يَقُوْلُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(47)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASTAMEU’OONA BEHI IZ YASTAMEU’OONA ELAYKA WA IZ HUM NAJWAAA IZ YAQOOLO ZAALEMOON IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA RAJULAN MMASHOORAN.\nWe know best why it is they listen, when they listen to thee; and when they meet in private conference, behold, the wicked say, “Ye follow none other than a man bewitched!” \nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلًا‏(48)\nAUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOOA LAKA AL-AAMSAALA FAZALLOOA FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAA.\nSee what similes they strike for thee: but they have gone astray, and never can they find a way. \nوَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(49)\nWA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN WWARUFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON KHALQAN JADEEDAN.\nThey say: “What! when we are reduced to bones and dust, should we really be raised up (to be) a new creation?” \nقُلْ كُوْنُوْا حِجَارَةً اَوْ حَدِيْدًا‏(50)\nQUL KOONOO HEJAARATAN AW HADEEDAN.\nSay: “(Nay!) be ye stones or iron, \nاَوْ خَلْقًا مِّمَّا يَكْبُرُ فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْۚ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَنْ يُّعِيْدُنَا ؕ قُلِ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ۚ فَسَيُنْغِضُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ رُءُوْسَهُمْ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هُوَ ؕ قُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ قَرِيْبًا‏(51)\nAW KHALQAN MIMMAA YAKBURU FEE SUDOOREKUM FASAYAQOOLOONA MAN YYUE’EEDUNAA QOLIL LAZEE FATARAKUM AWWALA MARRAH FASAYUNGHEZOONA ELAYKA RO-OOSAHUM WA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HOWA QUL A’SAA AN YAKOONA QAREEBAA.\n“Or created matter which, in your minds, is hardest (to be raised up), (Yet shall ye be raised up)!” then will they say: “Who will cause us to return?” Say: “He who created you first!” Then will they wag their heads towards thee, and say, “When will that be?” Say, “May be it will be quite soon! \nيَوْمَ يَدْعُوْكُمْ فَتَسْتَجِيْبُوْنَ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَتَظُنُّوْنَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(52)\nYAWMA YADU’OOKUM FATASTAJEEBOONA BEHAMDEH HANAAJERA WA IN LLABESTUM ILLAA QALEELAA.\n“It will be on a Day when He will call you, and ye will answer (His call) with (words of) His praise, and ye will think that ye tarried but a little while!” \nوَقُلْ لِّعِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوا الَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ يَنْزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ عَدُوًّا مُّبِيْنًا‏(53)\nWA QUL LLEE’EBAADEAA YAQOOLOOA LATEE HEYA AAHSANU INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA YANZAGHU BAYNAHUM INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA KAANA INSAANIK A’DUWWAL MOBEENAA.\nSay to My servants that they should (only) say those things that are best: for Satan doth sow dissensions among them: For Satan is to man an avowed enemy. \nرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يَرْحَمْكُمْ اَوْ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُعَذِّبْكُمْ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيْلًا‏(54)\nRABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEKUM IN YYASHAA YARHAMKUM AW IN YYASHAA QABLO WA MAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM WAKEELAA.\nIt is your Lord that knoweth you best: If He please, He granteth you mercy, or if He please, punishment: We have not sent thee to be a disposer of their affairs for them. \nوَرَبُّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَلَقَدْ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَ النَّبِيّٖنَ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّاٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ زَبُوْرًا‏(55)\nWA RABBOKA A-A’LAMO BEMAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA LAQAD FAZZALNAA YAWM NABIYYEENA A’LAA ELAA WWAATAYNAA DAAWOODA ZABOORAN.\nAnd it is your Lord that knoweth best all beings that are in the heavens and on earth: We did bestow on some prophets more (and other) gifts than on others: and We gave to David (the gift of) the Psalms. \nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنْكُمْ وَلَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(56)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM MIN DOONEHI FALAA YAMLEKOONA KASHFA AZ-ZURRE A’NKUM WA LAA TAHWEELAN.\nSay: “Call on those - besides Him - whom ye fancy: they have neither the power to remove your troubles from you nor to change them.” \nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمُ الْوَسِيْلَةَ اَيُّهُمْ اَقْرَبُ وَيَرْجُوْنَ رَحْمَتَهٗ وَيَخَافُوْنَ عَذَابَهٗؕ اِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ كَانَ مَحْذُوْرًا‏(57)\nAOOLAAEKA LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA YABTAGHOONA ELAA RABBEHEMU AL-WASEELATA AAYHUM AQRABO WA YARJOON RAHMATAH WA YAKHAAFOONA A’AZAABAH INNA A’ZAABAL RABBEKA KAANA MAHZOORAN.\nThose whom they call upon do desire (for themselves) means of access to their Lord, - even those who are nearest: they hope for His Mercy and fear His Wrath: for the Wrath of thy Lord is something to take heed of. \nوَاِنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا نَحْنُ مُهْلِكُوْهَا قَبْلَ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَوْ مُعَذِّبُوْهَا عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ كَانَ ذٰ لِكَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَسْطُوْرًا‏(58)\nWA MIN QARYATINW ILLAA NAHNO MUHLEKOOHAA QABLA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE AW MUA’AZZEBOOHAA A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA KAANA ZAA LEKA FIL KETAABE MASTOORAN.\nThere is not a population but We shall destroy it before the Day of Judgment or punish it with a dreadful Penalty: that is written in the (eternal) Record. \nوَمَا مَنَعَنَاۤ اَنْ نُّرْسِلَ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ كَذَّبَ بِهَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ وَاٰتَيْنَا ثَمُوْدَ النَّاقَةَ مُبْصِرَةً فَظَلَمُوْا بِهَاؕ وَمَا نُرْسِلُ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّا تَخْوِيْفًا‏(59)\nWA MAA MANAA’ANAA AN NNURSELA BE-AAYAATE ILLAA AN KAZZABA BEHAL AL-AAWLOONA WA AATAYNAA ELAA AN-NAAQATA MUBSERATAN FA ZALAMOO BEHAA WA MAA NURSELU BE-AAYAATE ILLAA TAKHWEEFAN.\nAnd We refrain from sending the signs, only because the men of former generations treated them as false: We sent the she-camel to the Thamud to open their eyes, but they treated her wrongfully: We only send the Signs by way of terror (and warning from evil). \nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لَكَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ اَحَاطَ بِالنَّاسِ ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّءْيَا الَّتِىْۤ اَرَيْنٰكَ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَ الشَّجَرَةَ الْمَلْعُوْنَةَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَنُخَوِّفُهُمْۙ فَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا طُغْيَانًا كَبِيْرًا‏(60)\nWA IZ QULNAL LAKA INNAL RABBAKA AHAATAL BIN-NAASE WA MAA JA-A’LNAA RO-YAA LATEE AARAYNAAKA ILLAA FETNATAN LIN-NAASE WAL SHAJARATA AL-MALU’OONATA FIL QUR-AANE WANUKHAWFUHUM FAMAA YAZEEDUHUM ILLAA TUGHYAANAN KABEERAA.\nBehold! We told thee that thy Lord doth encompass mankind round about: We granted the vision which We showed thee, but as a trial for men, as also the Cursed Tree (mentioned) in the Qur'an: We put terror (and warning) into them, but it only increases their inordinate transgression! \nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَ قَالَ ءَاَسْجُدُ لِمَنْ خَلَقْتَ طِيْنًا ۚ‏(61)\nWA IZ QULNAL LIL-MALAAEKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA AEBLEESA QAALA AASJUDU LEMAN-Y KHALAQTA TEENAN.\nBehold! We said to the angels: “Bow down unto Adam”: They bowed down except Iblis: He said, “Shall I bow down to one whom Thou didst create from clay?” \nقَالَ اَرَءَيْتَكَ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كَرَّمْتَ عَلَىَّ لَئِنْ اَخَّرْتَنِ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَاَحْتَنِكَنَّ ذُرِّيَّتَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(62)\nQAALA AARAAYTAKA HAAZAL LAZEE KARRAMTA A’LAYYA LAIL AAKKHARTANE ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAAHTANEKANNA ZURREETAH ILLAA QALEELAA.\nHe said: “Seest Thou? this is the one whom Thou hast honoured above me! If Thou wilt but respite me to the Day of Judgment, I will surely bring his descendants under my sway - all but a few!” \nقَالَ اذْهَبْ فَمَنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ جَزَآؤُكُمْ جَزَآءً مَّوْفُوْرًا‏(63)\nQAALA AZHAB FAMAN TABEA’AKA MINHUM FA-INNAL JAHANNAMA JAZAAUKUM JA-ZAAA-AWN MMAWFOORAN.\n(Allah) said: “Go thy way; if any of them follow thee, verily Hell will be the recompense of you (all)- an ample recompense. \nوَاسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُمْ بِصَوْتِكَ وَاَجْلِبْ عَلَيْهِمْ بِخَيْلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ وَشَارِكْهُمْ فِى الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَوْلَادِ وَعِدْهُمْ ؕ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(64)\nWAASTAFZEZ MANIS ASTATAA’TA MINHUM BESAWTEKA WAAJLEB A’LAYHIM BEKHAYLEKA WARAJELEKA WASHAAREKHUM FIL AMWAALE WAL WAL AAWLAADE WAE’EDHUM WA MAA YAE’EDUHUMU SHAYTAANO ILLAA GHOROORAA.\n“Lead to destruction those whom thou canst among them, with thy (seductive) voice; make assaults on them with thy cavalry and thy infantry; mutually share with them wealth and children; and make promises to them.” But Satan promises them nothing but deceit. \nاِنَّ عِبَادِىْ لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنٌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ وَكِيْلًا‏(65)\nINNA E’BAADEE LAYSA LAKA A’LAYHIM SULTAANUN KAFAA BERABBEKA WAKEELAA.\n“As for My servants, no authority shalt thou have over them:” Enough is thy Lord for a Disposer of affairs. \nرَبُّكُمُ الَّذِىْ يُزْجِىْ لَكُمُ الْفُلْكَ فِى الْبَحْرِ لِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيْمًا‏(66)\nRABBUKUMU LAZEE YUZJEAA LAKOMUL AL-FULKA FIL BAHRE LE-TABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEH INNAHU KAANA BEKUM RAHEEMAA.\nYour Lord is He That maketh the Ship go smoothly for you through the sea, in order that ye may seek of his Bounty. For he is unto you most Merciful. \nوَاِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فِى الْبَحْرِ ضَلَّ مَنْ تَدْعُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮكُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ اَعْرَضْتُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ كَفُوْرًا‏(67)\nWA EZAA MASSAKUMU AZ-ZURRU FIL BAHRE ZALLA MAN TADU’OONA ILLAA IYYAAHO FALAMMAA NAJJAAKUM ELAL BARRE AAA’RAZTUM KAANAL INSAANO KAFOORAA.\nWhen distress seizes you at sea, those that ye call upon - besides Himself - leave you in the lurch! but when He brings you back safe to land, ye turn away (from Him). Most ungrateful is man! \nاَفَاَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ بِكُمْ جَانِبَ الْبَرِّ اَوْ يُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ حَاصِبًا ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْالَكُمْ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(68)\nAAFAAMENTUM AN YAKHSEFA BEKUM JAANEBA BARRE AW YURSELA A’LAYKUM HAASEBAN SUMMA LAA TAJEDOOALAKUM WAKEELAA.\nDo ye then feel secure that He will not cause you to be swallowed up beneath the earth when ye are on land, or that He will not send against you a violent tornado (with showers of stones) so that ye shall find no one to carry out your affairs for you? \nاَمْ اَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يُّعِيْدَكُمْ فِيْهِ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى فَيُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ قَاصِفًا مِّنَ الرِّيْحِ فَيُغْرِقَكُمْ بِمَا كَفَرْتُمْۙ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْا لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا بِهٖ تَبِيْعًا‏(69)\nAM AMINTUM AN YYUE’EEDAKUM FEEHE TAARATAN LAHU FAYURSELA A’LAYKUM QAASEFAN MENAL AR-REEHE FAYUGHREQAKUM BEMAA KAFARTUM SUMMA LAA WA LAM LAKUM A’LAYNAA BEHI TABEEA’AN.\nOr do ye feel secure that He will not send you back a second time to sea and send against you a heavy gale to drown you because of your ingratitude, so that ye find no helper. Therein against Us? \nوَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ وَحَمَلْنٰهُمْ فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقْنَا تَفْضِيْلًا‏(70)\nWA LAQAD KARRAMNAA BANEE AADAMAL WAHAMALNAAHUM FIL BARRE WAL BAHRE WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAFAZZALNAAHUM A’LAA KASEERIM MIMMAYN KHALAQNAL TAFZEELAN.\nWe have honoured the sons of Adam; provided them with transport on land and sea; given them for sustenance things good and pure; and conferred on them special favours, above a great part of our creation. \nيَوْمَ نَدْعُوْا كُلَّ اُنَاسٍۢ بِاِمَامِهِمْۚ فَمَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ يَقْرَءُوْنَ كِتٰبَهُمْ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(71)\nYAWMA NADU’OOA KULLA ONAASIM BEAEMAAMEHEM FAMAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI FAAWLAAEKA YAQRAOONA KETAABAHUM WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nOne day We shall call together all human beings with their (respective) Imams: those who are given their record in their right hand will read it (with pleasure), and they will not be dealt with unjustly in the least. \nوَمَنْ كَانَ فِىْ هٰذِهٖۤ اَعْمٰى فَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْمٰى وَاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(72)\nWA MAN KAANA FEE HAAZEHI AAA’MAA FAHOWA FIL AAKHERATE AAA’MAA WA AZALLO SABEELAA.\nBut those who were blind in this world, will be blind in the hereafter, and most astray from the Path. \nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَفْتِنُوْنَكَ عَنِ الَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ لِتَفْتَرِىَ عَلَيْنَا غَيْرَهٗ ۖ  وَاِذًا لَّاتَّخَذُوْكَ خَلِيْلًا‏(73)\nWA KAADOO LAYAFTENOONAKA A’NIL LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA LETAFTAREAAA A’LAYNAA GHAYRAH WA EZAL LLAATTAKHAZOOKA KHALEELAN.\nAnd their purpose was to tempt thee away from that which We had revealed unto thee, to substitute in our name something quite different; (in that case), behold! they would certainly have made thee (their) friend! \nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ ثَبَّتْنٰكَ لَقَدْ كِدْتَّ تَرْكَنُ اِلَيْهِمْ شَيْئًا قَلِيْلًا  ۙ‏(74)\nWA LAWLAA AN SABBATNAAKA LAQAD KEDTTA TARKANU ELAYHIM SHAY-ANW QALEELAA.\nAnd had We not given thee strength, thou wouldst nearly have inclined to them a little. \nاِذًا لَّاَذَقْنٰكَ ضِعْفَ الْحَيٰوةِ وَضِعْفَ الْمَمَاتِ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ عَلَيْنَا نَصِيْرًا‏(75)\nEZAL LLAAZAQNAAKA ZEA’FA HAYAATID WAZEA’FA AL-MAMAATE SUMMA LAA TAJEDU LAKA A’LAYNAA NASEERAA.\nIn that case We should have made thee taste an equal portion (of punishment) in this life, and an equal portion in death: and moreover thou wouldst have found none to help thee against Us! \nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَسْتَفِزُّوْنَكَ مِنَ الْاَرْضِ لِيُخْرِجُوْكَ مِنْهَا وَاِذًا لَّا يَلْبَثُوْنَ خِلٰفَكَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(76)\nWA KAADOO LAYASTAFEZZOONAKA MENAL ARZE LEEKHREJOOKA MINHAA WA EZAL LAA YALBASOONA KHELAAFAKA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nTheir purpose was to scare thee off the land, in order to expel thee; but in that case they would not have stayed (therein) after thee, except for a little while. \nسُنَّةَ مَنْ قَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنْ رُّسُلِنَا وَلَا تَجِدُ لِسُنَّتِنَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(77)\nSUNNATAL MAN QAD ARSALNAA QABLAKA MIR RRUSULENAA WA LAA TAJEDU LESUNNATENAA TAHWEELAN.\n(This was Our) way with the messengers We sent before thee: thou wilt find no change in Our ways. \nاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِدُلُوْكِ الشَّمْسِ اِلٰى غَسَقِ الَّيْلِ وَقُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِؕ اِنَّ قُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِ كَانَ مَشْهُوْدًا‏(78)\nAAQEME SALAATA LEDULOOKE ASH-SHAMSE ELAA GHASAQE LAYLE WAQURAAANA FAJR INNAL QURAAANA FAJR KAANA MASHHOODAN.\nEstablish regular prayers - at the sun's decline till the darkness of the night, and the morning prayer and reading: for the prayer and reading in the morning carry their testimony. \nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَتَهَجَّدْ بِهٖ نَافِلَةً لَّكَ ۖ  عَسٰۤى اَنْ يَّبْعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامًا مَّحْمُوْدًا‏(79)\nWA MENAN LAYLE FATAHAJJAD BEHI NAAFELATAN LAKA A’SAA AN YYABA’ASAKA RABBOKA MAQAAMAN MMAHMOODAN.\nAnd pray in the small watches of the morning: (it would be) an additional prayer (or spiritual profit) for thee: soon will thy Lord raise thee to a Station of Praise and Glory! \nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَدْخِلْنِىْ مُدْخَلَ صِدْقٍ وَّ اَخْرِجْنِىْ مُخْرَجَ صِدْقٍ وَّاجْعَلْ لِّىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ سُلْطٰنًا نَّصِيْرًا‏(80)\nWA QUL RABBIL AADKHELNEAA MUDKHALA SEDQIN WA AAKHREJNEAA MUKHRAJA SEDQIN WWAAJA’AL LEE MIN LLADUNKA SULTAANAN NNASEERAN.\nSay: “O my Lord! Let my entry be by the Gate of Truth and Honour, and likewise my exit by the Gate of Truth and Honour; and grant me from Thy Presence an authority to aid (me).” \nوَقُلْ جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُؕ اِنَّ الْبَاطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوْقًا‏(81)\nWA QUL JAAA-A HAQQO WAZAHAQA AL-BAATELU INNAL AL-BAATELA KAANA ZAHOOQAN.\nAnd say: “Truth has (now) arrived, and Falsehood perished: for Falsehood is (by its nature) bound to perish.” \nوَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ مَا هُوَ شِفَآءٌ وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ وَلَا يَزِيْدُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ اِلَّا خَسَارًا‏(82)\nWANUNAZZELU MENAL QUR-AANE MAA HOWA SHEFAAUN WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN WA LAA YAZEEDU ZAALEMEEN ILLAA KHASAARAN.\nWe send down (stage by stage) in the Qur'an that which is a healing and a mercy to those who believe: to the unjust it causes nothing but loss after loss. \nوَاِذَاۤ اَنْعَمْنَا عَلَى الْاِنْسَانِ اَعْرَضَ وَنَاٰ بِجَانِبِهٖۚ وَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ كَانَ يَئُوْسًا‏(83)\nWA EZAA AN-A’MNAA A’LAL INSAANE A-A’RAZA WA NA-AA BEJAANEBEH WA EZAA MASSAHUSH SHARRO KAANA YAOOSAN.\nYet when We bestow Our favours on man, he turns away and becomes remote on his side (instead of coming to Us), and when evil seizes him he gives himself up to despair! \nقُلْ كُلٌّ يَّعْمَلُ عَلٰى شَاكِلَتِهٖؕ فَرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ هُوَ اَهْدٰى سَبِيْلًا‏(84)\nQUL KULLUL YYAA’MALU A’LAA SHAAKELATEH FA RABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAN HOWA AHDAA SABEELAA.\nSay: “Everyone acts according to his own disposition: But your Lord knows best who it is that is best guided on the Way.” \nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الرُّوْحِ ؕ قُلِ الرُّوْحُ مِنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّىْ وَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(85)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AR-ROOHE QOLIL ROOHO MIN AMRE RABBEE WA MAA MAA OOTEETUM MENAL I’LME ILLAA QALEELAA.\nThey ask thee concerning the Spirit (of inspiration). Say: “The Spirit (cometh) by command of my Lord: of knowledge it is only a little that is communicated to you, (O men!)” \nوَلَئِنْ شِئْنَا لَنَذْهَبَنَّ بِالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ بِهٖ عَلَيْنَا وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(86)\nWA LAIN SHE’NAA LANAZHABANNA BIL-LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA SUMMA LAA TAJEDU LAKA BEHI A’LAYNAA WAKEELAA.\nIf it were Our Will, We could take away that which We have sent thee by inspiration:then wouldst thou find none to plead thy affair in that matter as against Us, \nاِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ ؕ اِنَّ فَضْلَهٗ كَانَ عَلَيْكَ كَبِيْرًا‏(87)\nILLAA RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA INNAL FAZLAH KAANA A’LAYKA KABEERAA.\nExcept for Mercy from thy Lord: for his bounty is to thee (indeed) great. \nقُلْ لَّئِنِ اجْتَمَعَتِ الْاِنْسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتُوْا بِمِثْلِ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لَا يَاْتُوْنَ بِمِثْلِهٖ وَلَوْ كَانَ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ ظَهِيْرًا‏(88)\nQUL LLAENE AJTAMAA’ATE AL-AENSU WAL JENNU A’LAA AN YYAATOOA BE-MISLE HAAZAL QUR-AANE LAA YAATOONAL BEMESLEH WA LAW KAANA KHALAA LE-BA’ZIN ZAHEERAL.\nSay: “If the whole of mankind and Jinns were to gather together to produce the like of this Qur'an, they could not produce the like thereof, even if they backed up each other with help and support. \nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(89)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA LIN-NAASE FEE HAAZAL QUR-AANE MIN KULLE MASALIN FAABAAA AAKSARU NAASE ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nAnd We have explained to man, in this Qur'an, every kind of similitude: yet the greater part of men refuse (to receive it) except with ingratitude! \nوَقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتّٰى تَفْجُرَ لَنَا مِنَ الْاَرْضِ يَنْۢبُوْعًا ۙ‏(90)\nWA QAALOO LAN NOAMENA LAKA HATTAA TAFJURA LANAA MENAL ARZE YANBOOA’AN.\nThey say: “We shall not believe in thee, until thou cause a spring to gush forth for us from the earth, \nاَوْ تَكُوْنَ لَكَ جَنَّةٌ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّعِنَبٍ فَتُفَجِّرَ الْاَنْهٰرَ خِلٰلَهَا تَفْجِيْرًا ۙ‏(91)\nAW TAKOONA LAKA JANNATUM MIN NAKHEELINW WWAE’ENABIN FATUFAJJERA AL-AANHAARA JA-A’LA TAFJEERAN.\n“Or (until) thou have a garden of date trees and vines, and cause rivers to gush forth in their midst, carrying abundant water; \nاَوْ تُسْقِطَ السَّمَآءَ كَمَا زَعَمْتَ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا اَوْ تَاْتِىَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ قَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(92)\nAW TUSQETA SAMAAA-AD KAMAA ZAA’AMTA A’LAYNAA KESAFAN AW TAATEAAA BIL-LAAHE WAL MALAAEKATE QABEELAN.\n“Or thou cause the sky to fall in pieces, as thou sayest (will happen), against us; or thou bring Allah and the angels before (us) face to face: \nاَوْ يَكُوْنَ لَكَ بَيْتٌ مِّنْ زُخْرُفٍ اَوْ تَرْقٰى فِى السَّمَآءِ ؕ وَلَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لِرُقِيِّكَ حَتّٰى تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا كِتٰبًا نَّقْرَؤُهٗ ؕ قُلْ سُبْحَانَ رَبِّىْ هَلْ كُنْتُ اِلَّا بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(93)\nAW YAKOONA LAKA BAYTUN MIN ZUKHRUFIN AW TARQAA FIL SAMAAA-E WA LAN NOAMENA LERUQEEKA HATTAA TUNAZZELA A’LAYNAA KETAABAA NNAQRAUH QUL SUBHAANA RABBEE HAL KUNTO ILLAA BASHARAN RASOOLANY.\n“Or thou have a house adorned with gold, or thou mount a ladder right into the skies. No, we shall not even believe in thy mounting until thou send down to us a book that we could read.” Say: “Glory to my Lord! Am I aught but a man, a messenger?” \nوَمَا مَنَعَ النَّاسَ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْۤا اِذْ جَآءَهُمُ الْهُدٰٓى اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(94)\nWA MAA MANAA’A NAASA AN YOAMENOO IZ JAAA-AHOMUL HODAA ILLAA AN QAALOO AABAA’ASA LAAHO BASHARAN RASOOLANY.\nWhat kept men back from belief when Guidance came to them, was nothing but this: they said, “Has Allah sent a man (like us) to be (His) Messenger?” \nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَلٰۤئِكَةٌ يَّمْشُوْنَ مُطْمَئِنِّيْنَ لَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَلَكًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(95)\nQUL LAW KAANA FIL ARZE MALAAEKATUN YYAMSHOONA MUTMAENNEENA LANAZZALNAA A’LAYHIM MENAL SAMAAA-E MALAKAN RASOOLANY.\nSay, “If there were settled, on earth, angels walking about in peace and quiet, We should certainly have sent them down from the heavens an angel for a messenger.” \nقُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(96)\nQUL KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nSay: “Enough is Allah for a witness between me and you: for He is well acquainted with His servants, and He sees (all things). \nوَمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ ؕ وَنَحْشُرُهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ عُمْيًا وَّبُكْمًا وَّصُمًّا ؕ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ ؕ كُلَّمَا خَبَتْ زِدْنٰهُمْ سَعِيْرًا‏(97)\nWA MAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAHOWA AL-MUHTADE WA MAN YYUZLEL FALAN TAJEDA LAHUM AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONEHI WANAHSHURUHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE A’LAA SEEMAAHUM U’UMYAN WWABUKMAN WWASUMMAN MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL KULLAMAA KHABAT ZEDNAAHUM SA-E’ERAA.\nIt is he whom Allah guides, that is on true Guidance; but he whom He leaves astray - for such wilt thou find no protector besides Him. On the Day of Judgment We shall gather, them together, prone on their faces, blind, dumb, and deaf: their abode will be Hell: every time it shows abatement, We shall increase from them the fierceness of the Fire. \nذٰلِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(98)\nZAALEKA JAZAAUHUM BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENAA WA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN WWARUFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON KHALQAN JADEEDAN.\nThat is their recompense, because they rejected Our signs, and said, “When we are reduced to bones and broken dust, should we really be raised up (to be) a new Creation?” \nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّخْلُقَ مِثْلَهُمْ وَجَعَلَ لَهُمْ اَجَلًا لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ ؕ فَاَبَى الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(99)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAL LAAHA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA QAADERUN A’LAA AN ANY-YAKHLOQA MESLAHUM WA LAHUM AAJALAN LAA RAYBA FEEHE FAABAA ZAALEMOON ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nSee they not that Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth, has power to create the like of them (anew)? Only He has decreed a term appointed, of which there is no doubt. But the unjust refuse (to receive it) except with ingratitude. \nقُلْ لَّوْ اَنْتُمْ تَمْلِكُوْنَ خَزَآئِنَ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّاَمْسَكْتُمْ خَشْيَةَ الْاِنْفَاقِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ قَتُوْرًا‏(100)\nQUL LAW ANTUM TAMLEKOONA KHAZAAENA RAHMATE RABBEE EZAL LLAAMSAKTUM KHASHYATA AL-AENFAAQE KAANAL INSAANO QATOORAN.\nSay: “If ye had control of the Treasures of the Mercy of my Lord, behold, ye would keep them back, for fear of spending them: for man is (every) niggardly!” \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى تِسْعَ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ فَسْئَلْ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ فَقَالَ لَهٗ فِرْعَوْنُ اِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰمُوْسٰى مَسْحُوْرًا‏(101)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAA TESA’A AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT FASAL BANEE AESRAAEELA IZ JAAA-AHUM FAQAALA LAHU FIRA’WNO INNEE LAAZUNNUKA YAA MOOSAA MASHOORAN.\nTo Moses We did give Nine Clear Signs: As the Children of Israel: when he came to them, Pharaoh said to him: “O Moses! I consider thee, indeed, to have been worked upon by sorcery! \nقَالَ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِلَّا رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ بَصَآئِرَ ۚ وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰفِرْعَوْنُ مَثْبُوْرًا‏(102)\nQAALA LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA ANZALAL HAAOOLAAA-E ILLAA RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE BASAAA-ERA WA INNEE LAAZUNNUKA YAA FIRA’WNO MASBOORAN.\nMoses said, “Thou knowest well that these things have been sent down by none but the Lord of the heavens and the earth as eye-opening evidence: and I consider thee indeed, O Pharaoh, to be one doomed to destruction!” \nفَاَرَادَ اَنْ يَّسْتَفِزَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُ وَ مَنْ مَّعَهٗ جَمِيْعًا ۙ‏(103)\nFA ARAADA AN YYASTAFEZZAHUM MENAL ARZE FAAGHRAQNAAHU WA MAN MMAA’AH JAMEE-A’A.\nSo he resolved to remove them from the face of the earth: but We did drown him and all who were with him. \nوَّقُلْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ لِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اسْكُنُوا الْاَرْضَ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ جِئْنَا بِكُمْ لَفِيْفًا ؕ‏(104)\nWWAQULNAA MIN BA’DEHI LE-BANEE AESRAAEELA ASKUNOOA ARZA FA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AAKHERATE JENAA BEKUM LAFEEFAN.\nAnd We said thereafter to the Children of Israel, “Dwell securely in the land (of promise)”: but when the second of the warnings came to pass, We gathered you together in a mingled crowd. \nوَبِالْحَقِّ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ وَبِالْحَقِّ نَزَلَ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا ۘ‏(105)\nWA BIL-HAQQE ANZALNAAHO WA BIL-HAQQE NAZALA WA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MUBASSHERAN WA NAZEERANW.\nWe sent down the (Qur'an) in Truth, and in Truth has it descended: and We sent thee but to give Glad Tidings and to warn (sinners). \nوَقُرْاٰنًا فَرَقْنٰهُ لِتَقْرَاَهٗ عَلَى النَّاسِ عَلٰى مُكْثٍ وَّنَزَّلْنٰهُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(106)\nWA QURAANAN FARAQNAAHU LETAQRAAH A’LAL NAASE A’LAA MUKSIN WWANAZZALNAAHU TANZEELAA.\n(It is) a Qur'an which We have divided (into parts from time to time), in order that thou mightest recite it to men at intervals: We have revealed it by stages. \nقُلْ اٰمِنُوْا بِهٖۤ اَوْ لَا تُؤْمِنُوْٓا ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖۤ اِذَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ يَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ سُجَّدًا ۙ‏(107)\nQUL AAMENOO BEHI AW LAA TUMENOOA INNAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA MIN QABLEHI EZAA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM YAKHERROONA LIL-AAZQAANE SUJJADANW.\nSay: “Whether ye believe in it or not, it is true that those who were given knowledge beforehand, when it is recited to them, fall down on their faces in humble prostration, \nوَّيَقُوْلُوْنَ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَاۤ اِنْ كَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّنَا لَمَفْعُوْلًا‏(108)\nWWAYAQOOLOONA LAAHE RABBENAA IN KAANA WAA’DU RABBENAA LAMAFU’OOLAN.\n“And they say: 'Glory to our Lord! Truly has the promise of our Lord been fulfilled!'“ \nوَيَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ يَبْكُوْنَ وَيَزِيْدُهُمْ خُشُوْعًا ۩‏(109)\nWAYAKHERROONA LIL-AAZQAANE YABKOONA WAYAZEEDUHUM KHUSHOOA’AN.\nThey fall down on their faces in tears, and it increases their (earnest) humility. [۩] \nقُلِ ادْعُوا اللّٰهَ اَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمٰنَ ؕ اَ يًّا مَّا تَدْعُوْا فَلَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى ۚ وَلَا تَجْهَرْ بِصَلَاتِكَ وَلَا تُخَافِتْ بِهَا وَابْتَغِ بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ سَبِيْلًا‏(110)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAAHA AWE’ ADU’OOA BIL-GHAYBE AAYA MAA TADU’OOA FA LAHUL ASMAA-UL AL-HUSNAA WA LAA TAJHAR BESALAATEKA WA LAA TUKHAAFET BEHAA WABTAGHE BAYNA ZAA LEKA SABEELAA.\nSay: “Call upon Allah, or call upon Rahman: by whatever name ye call upon Him, (it is well): for to Him belong the Most Beautiful Names. Neither speak thy Prayer aloud, nor speak it in a low tone, but seek a middle course between.” \nوَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِىٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا‏(111)\nWA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE LAM YATTAKHEZ LAAHO LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL AL-MULKE WA LAM YAKUL LAHU WALIYYUN MENAL AZ-ZULLE WAKABBERHU TAKBEERAN.\nSay: “Praise be to Allah, who begets no son, and has no partner in (His) dominion: Nor (needs) He any to protect Him from humiliation: yea, magnify Him for His greatness and glory!” ",
  "merits": "Surah Bani Israaeel\nThere are 111 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a great reward will be accorded to those who recite this Surah and when they reach the verse about parents, they feel a sense of love and gentleness towards their parents.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah Bani Israeel every Thursday night, will not die before meeting Imam Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) and will be counted among his companions. Also, if a child is not able to speak or is delaying in his learning how to speak, he should be given the water of this Surah that has been written with saffron.\nIn the commentary of Safi it is written that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) told Imam Ali (a.s.) that the last two verses of this Surah are a protection and safety from theft. This Surah is also called Surah al-Isra’."
